      "summaryMarkdown": "All three findings are repaired and verified in source and tests. Non-root Root steps now authenticate with an interactive `sudo -v` first; a refused prompt returns Declined without running the command, a failing wrapped command stays an ordinary failure, and the fake-sudo tests prove the argv, env, cwd, decline and Print-never-calls-sudo paths (Unix-only, run under WSL by the coordinator and compiled out on Windows). The WM_SETTINGCHANGE broadcast is best-effort with a failing-broadcast test. quote_windows follows CommandLineToArgvW rules and is covered by a rendering test. REPO-1, REPO-3, HOST-1, HOST-2, HOST-3 are proven by their own groups; REPO-2's workflow matches the criterion and its first green run awaits the first push.",
