  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "F-HOST2-SUDO-DECLINE",
      "criterionIds": [
        "HOST-2"
      ],
      "severity": "major",
      "status": "resolved",
      "descriptionMarkdown": "**Expected (HOST-2):** a `Root` step on Linux/macOS runs through `sudo` when not root, and declining the `sudo` prompt stops the step with a clear message, not a crash; the check description requires this to be proven by `tests/command_runner.rs`.\n\n**Observed:** `src/host/runner.rs:374-382` maps a declined `sudo` to `RunError::Declined` only when the sudo process has no exit code (killed by a signal). Real declines do not take that path: a failed or empty password, Ctrl+D or `sudo: a password is required` all make `sudo` exit with code 1, which is returned as an ordinary `Outcome` (and `run_checked` reports `` `sudo ...` exited with code 1`` with no mention of a declined prompt for interactive specs). Ctrl+C sends SIGINT to the whole foreground process group, so `rayx` itself dies before it can map anything. The Declined branch is therefore effectively unreachable. In addition, `sudo_wrapped` (`runner.rs:439-455`: `env K=V` forwarding, cwd, inherited stdin) and the `Privilege::Root` execute branch have no test at all: `tests/command_runner.rs` covers sudo only as a printed string (Print mode) and the already-root direct path, and the declined case only through the scripted `Elevator` (the Windows/UAC half). The `sudo` half of the last HOST-2 bullet is thus neither correctly implemented nor proven.\n\n**Repair:** (1) Before running a `Root` step as non-root, authenticate with an interactive, console-inheriting `sudo -v` (still no password handling by `rayx`); a non-zero exit from `sudo -v` is a refused/declined prompt and returns `RunError::Declined` with the existing clear message, while a non-zero exit of the wrapped command stays a normal failure. Keep the signal case as Declined too. (2) Add `#[cfg(unix)]` tests in `tests/command_runner.rs` that put a fake `sudo` shell script in a temporary directory on `PATH` (or unit-test `sudo_wrapped`) to prove the argv (`sudo env K=V program args`), cwd propagation, that a failing fake `sudo -v` yields `Declined` with the 'did not run' message and does not run the command, and that an approving one runs the command. Print mode must stay side-effect free.",
      "regressionRefs": [
        {
          "repositoryId": "rayx-cli",
          "path": "src/host/runner.rs",
          "symbol": "Runner::execute_spec"
        },
        {
          "repositoryId": "rayx-cli",
          "path": "tests/command_runner.rs",
          "symbol": "fake_sudo"
        }
      ],
      "boundaryId": "s1-foundation"
    },
    {
      "id": "F-HOST3-BROADCAST-ERR",
      "criterionIds": [
        "HOST-3"
      ],
      "severity": "minor",
      "status": "resolved",
      "descriptionMarkdown": "**Expected:** the persisted PATH edit is the outcome; `WM_SETTINGCHANGE` is a best-effort notification, and `rayx` tells the user to open a new shell.\n\n**Observed:** `prepend_to_windows_path` (`src/host/path_env.rs:190-191`) returns `Err` when `broadcast_change` fails, and `RegistryPathStore::broadcast_change` (`path_env.rs:494-496`) returns an error whenever `SendMessageTimeoutW` returns 0, which also happens on a timeout caused by one slow top-level window (with `GetLastError` possibly 0). The registry value has then already been written, so the caller reports a failed step for a change that took effect, and a retry says `AlreadyPresent` without broadcasting.\n\n**Repair:** make the broadcast non-fatal (ignore or return it separately, for example as a warning field on the result), keeping the `Added` result and the new-shell notice; add a `MemoryPathStore` test with a failing broadcast showing `Added` is still returned.",
