      "severity": "minor",
      "status": "resolved",
      "descriptionMarkdown": "**Expected:** the command line `WindowsElevator` builds runs the argument it was given.\n\n**Observed:** `quote_windows` (`src/host/runner.rs:565-575`) wraps an argument containing spaces in quotes without doubling backslashes that precede the closing quote, so a directory argument such as `C:\\Program Files\\Tool\\` becomes `\"C:\\Program Files\\Tool\\\"`, which the target program's command-line parser reads as an escaped quote. The elevator already rejects `\"`, `%` and line breaks for this class of problem but not this one; `render` (Print) has the same text, so `--check` would show a line that does not match what really runs.\n\n**Repair:** double the run of backslashes that precedes a closing (or embedded) quote in `quote_windows`, or have the elevator refuse an argument ending in a backslash that needs quoting; add a case to the Windows elevator guard test or a pure `command_line` rendering test.",
